## Branching policy (NON-NEGOTIABLE)

**Branch shape:**

```
<prefix>/<git-username>/<slug>           # e.g. feature/lehidalgo/add-csv-export
<prefix>/<git-username>/<TICKET>-<slug>  # e.g. feature/lehidalgo/{{ ticket_prefix }}-142-add-csv-export
```

| Prefix | Branched from | PR target | Reviewers | Use case |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `feature/` | `{{ integration_branch }}` | `{{ integration_branch }}` | 1 | New feature |
| `bugfix/` | `{{ integration_branch }}` | `{{ integration_branch }}` | 1 | Non-urgent bug fix |
| `chore/` | `{{ integration_branch }}` | `{{ integration_branch }}` | 1 | Tooling, deps, docs |
| `release/` | `{{ integration_branch }}` | `{{ production_branch }}` | 2 | Release PR |
| `hotfix/` | `{{ production_branch }}` | `{{ production_branch }}` (then back-merge to `{{ integration_branch }}`) | 1 (fast) | Production fix |

The `<git-username>` segment is `git config user.name`, normalised to lowercase kebab. It enforces ownership across contributors.

### Forbidden actions for the agent

- Direct push to `{{ production_branch }}`, `main`, or `{{ integration_branch }}` — three-layer block (pre-push hook, Claude deny-list, GitHub branch protection).
- `git commit --no-verify` / `git push --no-verify` / `git commit -n` — if a hook is wrong, fix the hook.
- `git push --force` — use `--force-with-lease` (refuses if remote moved).
- Checking out `{{ production_branch }}` / `{{ integration_branch }}` — stay on a feature branch and use `git fetch + git merge origin/<branch>` to integrate.
- `git reset --hard` / `git clean -f` / `git checkout .` — destructive.
- `git config --global` modifications.
- `pip install` (use `uv add`).
- `npm install` without lockfile.
- Editing `.env` / `.env.*` (only `.env.example` is committed).
- Editing generated files: `routeTree.gen.ts`{% if has_typescript %}, `{{ frontend_dir }}/src/client/*`{% endif %}, `*.lock`, `*_pb2.py`, `.copier-answers.yml`.
- Adding `Co-Authored-By: Claude` (or any model attribution) to commit messages, code comments, or docs.
