## Branching policy (LIGHTWEIGHT)

This repository uses a **single-branch flow**: all work lands on `{{ production_branch }}`. Releases are managed by `release-please` (or equivalent) — direct pushes by maintainers are permitted but discouraged in favour of PRs.

The full `<prefix>/<git-username>/<slug>` policy is **not enforced** — the consumer opted out via `enable_branch_policy: false` in `.copier-answers.yml`. To re-enable later, set the flag to `true` and run `copier update`.

### Forbidden actions for the agent (still enforced)

- `git commit --no-verify` / `git push --no-verify` / `git commit -n` — if a hook is wrong, fix the hook.
- `git push --force` — use `--force-with-lease` (refuses if remote moved).
- `git reset --hard` / `git clean -f` / `git checkout .` — destructive.
- `git config --global` modifications.
- `pip install` (use `uv add`).
- `npm install` without lockfile.
- Editing `.env` / `.env.*` (only `.env.example` is committed).
- Editing generated files: `*.lock`, `*_pb2.py`, `.copier-answers.yml`.
- Adding `Co-Authored-By: Claude` (or any model attribution) to commit messages, code comments, or docs.
